# Reviewed source correction after stable-ID adoption (#1373)

This route corrects an exact finite set of source records in a **different real
Git checkout** while preserving the original completed adoption. It neither
replays adoption into that checkout nor edits the original receipt. The original
root, HEAD, origin, captured producer, scientific inputs and native endpoint are
verified through their own native producer before and after the correction.

The successor starts with the complete adopted owner/aggregate/ID-ledger bytes
and all four maintained mapping beforeimages, including explicit absences.
Original records, reviews and qualified historical evidence remain immutable.
The source correction writes only selected records, native aggregates and a
source-lineage marker. It leaves all four mapping files unchanged. A mapped to
unmapped correction may relocate the selected owner with exact retirement and
beforeimage evidence. Permanent MIM IDs, mint/lifecycle ledgers, all unselected
records, source accounting and inherited holds cannot change.

A selected correction can change grounding, its method/evidence, disproved
ontology-derived properties, primary unresolved status, documented aliases,
synonym dispositions and explanatory notes. It is not a merge/split, allocation,
composition, role, quantity or hold-release operator. The complete top-level
field delta and original attributed curation event are reviewed; an older
proposal timestamp is retained rather than rewritten to the batch timestamp.

An external identifier disproved for this owner must leave its resolving
`legacy_identifiers` and active identity/grounding fields. Its exact prior use
remains in immutable beforeimages, the declared delta and curation provenance.
A false raw label remains as native `REJECTED_LABEL` evidence, not a searchable
alias. A genuine historical placeholder may be restored as the selected primary
identifier, with collision checks and separate current scientific support.
These decisions are owner-scoped, never global deletion of the external term.

## Explicit inputs and native commands

The JSON request is closed and names the actual successor Git identity, exact
predecessor manifest/receipt/producer, all four mapping beforeimages, qualified
historical native review pairs, complete target owner/aggregate/ledger inventory,
original full source context, native Claw runtime, explicit operational policy
and exact correction proposals/evidence. `publication_proof` is explicitly null
when there is no prior native publication; otherwise it names that genuine
native manifest, receipt and producer. All earlier publication science pairs
must remain in qualified frozen history. A copied JSON success flag is not proof.

Run with the selected maintained Python 3.13 executable spelling and actual
`PYTHONPATH=<successor>/src`; use that same spelling for all subsequent phases.
The module CLI is the native entrypoint; no new justfile route is required:

```sh
python3 -m mediaingredientmech.curate.curation_successor inspect --root TARGET --request REQUEST
python3 -m mediaingredientmech.curate.curation_successor prepare --root TARGET --request ASSESSED_REQUEST --stage FRESH_STAGE
python3 -m mediaingredientmech.curate.curation_successor apply --root TARGET --stage FRESH_STAGE --acceptance ACCEPTANCE --receipt FRESH_RECEIPT
python3 -m mediaingredientmech.curate.curation_successor apply --root TARGET --stage FRESH_STAGE --acceptance ACCEPTANCE --receipt FRESH_RECEIPT --apply
python3 -m mediaingredientmech.curate.curation_successor verify --root TARGET --stage FRESH_STAGE --receipt FRESH_RECEIPT/application.json
```

Inspection returns actual payloads and target digests; it adds no decisions.
Publish those exact bytes using the existing guarded writer, then obtain one
current primary and a separate independent skeptical native review per selected
owner. Both must bind the complete delta, beforeimage, proposal, original source
context, policy, semantics and evidence. Required checks pass; corrective-delta
findings cannot remain open. Explicitly retained unrelated residual findings
and holds are recorded in both the payload and review dimensions, without a
release clearance. Native validate/save produces each actual YAML/Markdown pair.

The assessed request references those actual pairs and their input hashes.
Preparation reconstructs all native outputs and exporter roundtrip, then measures
the complete multi-root guards and backup cost. The forecast includes an actual
strict predecessor replay. No lease duration, namespace, fit age, safety factor
or overhead is changed implicitly. An independent native technical review must
accept the exact prepared manifest, full scientific input union, preserved
history, operational forecast, namespace and scheduling. Dry-run is read-only;
apply uses the existing lease, reservations and guarded writers. A failure keeps
partial observations and an invalidating FAILED receipt; no automatic resume,
lease renewal or reuse of a failed stage is supported.

## Generation and canonical publication are separate

Write a closed endpoint reference naming the actual completed successor stage,
manifest, receipt and recorded producer. Native generation explicitly selects it:

```sh
python3 -m mediaingredientmech.curate.stable_sssom_publication generate --root TARGET --claw-root CLAW --kg-root KG --stage FRESH_GENERATION --curation-successor ENDPOINT.json --curation-successor-sha256 SHA256
```

Do not also pass legacy adoption arguments. The genuine complete source chain
and all current inputs are verified before generation and again before its
success receipt. The actual native Claw triple is deterministically replayed;
no labels, mappings or approval are inferred from endpoint identity.

Canonical selection still needs current primary and separate skeptical
whole-row/suppression/history review, then independent exact-prepared-set
technical acceptance. Ordinary current external/source export review remains
separate. For a successor, publication additionally binds the complete local
correction proof and qualified predecessor closure into its reviews, manifest
and operational fit. All original historical obligations remain selected.

After canonical installation, use the native publication verifier. Only its
actual complete receipt can introduce the four authenticated archived mapping
beforeimages while the entire source/ID/review endpoint remains current. Its
full native reconstruction, actual paired reviews, technical acceptance,
operation accounting, fit and current canonical outputs must all pass before
success. A standalone source verifier still refuses changed mapping beforeimages;
naked archived maps, a foreign/partial receipt or self-rehashed rows cannot grant
publication authority. Source correction and installation confer no release,
ontology-identity, subclass, role, source-quantity or hold-clearance approval.

Completed verification permits an ordinary descendant commit while preserving the
original request, acquisition identity and producer attestation. Executable
source/runtime and every protected source, ID, review and output byte must still
match. It snapshots and guards the actually observed current HEAD/index; live
preparation/application still requires the exact selected baseline (#1378). Live
mint and lifecycle bytes are checked independently of their archived beforeimages
through all endpoint and publication boundaries (#1379).
